# Project Guidelines

Always reference and strictly adhere to the instructions defined in `AGENTS.md`
(`CLAUDE.md` is a symlink of it).

## i18n — CRITICAL (intentionally duplicated from AGENTS.md)
- Do NOT use Astro's native i18n routing. No localized subdirectories
  (`src/pages/en/`, `src/pages/es/`), no locale prefixes, no `i18n` option in
  `astro.config.mjs`. This project uses ONE route per page with a runtime
  language toggle (full rules in AGENTS.md).

## General Rules
- Do not hardcode static text directly inside `.astro` or UI components.
  Always use the translation dictionary (`src/i18n/ui.ts`) or data files
  (`src/data/`).
- Use TypeScript type-safety for translation keys and i18n helper parameters.
- Internal navigation links are plain and static; they never include locale
  prefixes and never change with the active language.
- When generating new pages or components, maintain consistency with the
  folder structure defined in `AGENTS.md`.